tuntap_bb: drop the Windows patch step and the tarball hash check

Two problems in dev_helper/tuntap_bb/CMakeLists.txt's FetchContent_Declare
for the vendored libtuntap, neither Windows-specific despite appearances:

- PATCH_COMMAND unconditionally runs `git apply ... libtuntap-win.patch`
  against the populated source, not gated behind `if(WIN32)` at all. On
  Linux that patch doesn't match anything, `git apply` (even with
  --reject) exits non-zero on a rejected hunk, and FetchContent treats
  that as a hard failure of the whole populate step.
- URL_HASH pins an MD5 of third_package/libtuntap.tar as originally
  shipped. This package's own AR8030_FIX_LIBTUNTAP_TARBALL pre-configure
  hook (ar8030.mk) rewrites that tarball to drop two hardcoded
  /usr/include, /usr/local/include entries that Buildroot's cross
  compiler wrapper refuses outright -- which changes its hash, so the
  pinned one no longer matches and FetchContent_Populate aborts with
  "MD5 hash ... does not match expected value" before ever reaching the
  patch step above.

Both only matter for a real multi-platform release process (verifying
the tarball hasn't drifted, patching Windows-only quirks) that this
project doesn't do for a third-party vendored dependency -- drop them
rather than try to keep either in sync with a tarball this package
already has to rewrite for cross-compilation.

diff --git a/dev_helper/tuntap_bb/CMakeLists.txt b/dev_helper/tuntap_bb/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/dev_helper/tuntap_bb/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/dev_helper/tuntap_bb/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -3,15 +3,11 @@

 include(FetchContent)

-set(winpatch git apply --ignore-whitespace --reject ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/third_package/libtuntap-win.patch)
-
 FetchContent_Declare(
     libtuntap
     DOWNLOAD_EXTRACT_TIMESTAMP YES
     URL ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/third_package/libtuntap.tar
-    URL_HASH MD5=a045bdf3199e3f185c7917f25eeeed5c
-    PATCH_COMMAND ${winpatch}
     UPDATE_DISCONNECTED 1
 )

 FetchContent_GetProperties(libtuntap)
